et\" is taken from Something Else by The Kinks, the band’s fifth album, released in September 1967. The album documents the band’s continuing interest in baroque pop, folk and music hall styles, led by Ray Davies’s trademark songwriting finesse. Produced by Ray himself, the record blends delicate harpsichord, brass, and organ arrangements with stories of British life, family, and reflection. It features two of the band’s most celebrated songs: “Waterloo Sunset,” often hailed as one of the greatest singles ever written, and Dave Davies’s “Death of a Clown,” which captures a mix of melancholy and charm. Something Else is intimate and wistful — a portrait of The Kinks at their most nuanced.\n\nThe legendary British band formed by Ray and Dave Davies in 1963, The Kinks helped shape rock music with their sharp songwriting and unforgettable riffs. From \"You Really Got Me\" to \"Come Dancing\" via \"Lola\", their influence was far reaching through heavy metal, power pop, and modern rock. Explore their timeless songs right here on the official Kinks channel.\n\nLyrics:\n\nDirty old river, must you keep rolling\nFlowing into the night\nPeople so busy, makes me feel dizzy\nTaxi light shines so bright\nBut I don't need no friends\nAs long as I gaze on Waterloo sunset\nI am in paradise\n\nEvery day I look at the world from my window\nBut chilly, chilly is the evening time\nWaterloo sunset's fine\n\nTerry meets Julie, Waterloo Station\nEvery Friday night\nBut I am so lazy, don't want to wander\nI stay at home at night\nBut I don't feel afraid\nAs long as I gaze on Waterloo sunset\nI am in paradise\n\nEvery day I look at the world from my window\nBut chilly, chilly is the evening time\nWaterloo sunset's fine\n\nMillions of people swarming like flies 'round Waterloo underground\nBut Terry and Julie cross over the river\nWhere they feel safe and sound\nAnd they don't need no friends\nAs long as they gaze on Waterloo sunset\nThey are in paradise\n\nWaterloo sunset's fine\n\n#TheKinks #WaterlooSunset #SomethingElse", "channel_id": "UC_NS3vx8ZLC6MPJJkBV1x9A", "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC_NS3vx8ZLC6MPJJkBV1x9A", "duration": 195, "view_count": 18124505, "age_limit": 0, "webpage_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=N_MqfF0WBsU", "categories": ["Music"], "tags": ["the kinks", "kinks", "lola kinks", "kinks songs", "the kinks songs", "ray davies", "dave davies", "best of the kinks", "you really got me", "waterloo sunset", "sunny afternoon", "the kinks lyrics", "The kinks", "The kinks kinks", "Kinks songs", "Kinks album", "The kinks supersonic rocket ship", "john gosling", "kinks band", "the kinks ray davies", "kinks chords", "kinks music", "one day", "one day netflix", "on day music", "one day netflix theme song", "netflix one day", "one day series", "one day 2023", "one day waterloo"], "playable_in_embed": true, "live_status": "not_live", "media_type": "video", "_format_sort_fields": ["quality", "res", "fps", "hdr:12", "source", "vcodec", "channels", "acodec", "lang", "proto"], "automatic_captions": {}, "subtitles": {}, "comment_count": 6600, "heatmap": [{"start_time": 0.0, "end_time": 1.96, "value": 1.0}, {"start_time": 1.96, "end_time": 3.92, "value": 0.5194050691796306}, {"start_time": 3.92, "end_time": 5.88, "value": 0.5309788299284166}, {"start_time": 5.88, "end_time": 7.84, "value": 0.5439785794410553}, {"start_time": 7.84, "end_time": 9.8, "value": 0.5496731217726415}, {"start_time": 9.8, "end_time": 11.76, "value": 0.5520906359734079}, {"start_time": 11.76, "end_time": 13.72, "value": 0.5314568562747084}, {"start_time": 13.72, "end_time": 15.68, "value": 0.5464278324130646}, {"start_time": 15.68, "end_time": 17.64, "value": 0.5156976228593833}, {"start_time": 17.64, "end_time": 19.6, "value": 0.5043720157386966}, {"start_time": 19.6, "end_time": 21.56, "value": 0.5000480749035001}, {"start_time": 21.56, "end_time": 23.52, "value": 0.4824531269690874}, {"start_time": 23.52, "end_time": 25.48, "value": 0.472621964785522